nodes.body:
The lint may generate uncompilable suggestion with `Applicability::MachineApplicable`. The applicability isn't shown in stderr so maybe I'm wrong and please check this locally.

---

Before:
```rust
let re: Result<(), _> = Err(Default::default());
let _ = re.map_or_else(|_: i32| 42, |_| 42);
```
The explicit i32 parameter type constrains the error type of re to i32.

After fix applied:
```rust
let re: Result<(), _> = Err(Default::default());
let _ = re.map_or(42, |_| 42);
```
We don't need type annotation in `map_or`, so the compiler doesn't know the `Result<(), _>` `_`'s type, which leads to `error[E0790]: cannot call associated function on trait without specifying the corresponding "impl" type`. 

I think `Applicability::MachineApplicable` may not fit, what about switch all the applicabilities to `Applicability::MaybeIncorrect`? Or you could also avoid this suggestion error by checking the `fn_decl.inputs`.

---

Maybe this patch could specifically downgrade when closures' parameters have a type annotation?
```suggestion
        let mut applicability = if body
            .params
            .iter()
            .all(|param| matches!(param.pat.kind, hir::PatKind::Binding(..) | hir::PatKind::Wild))
            && matches!(
                fn_decl.output,
                FnRetTy::DefaultReturn(_)
                    | FnRetTy::Return(hir::Ty {
                        kind: hir::TyKind::Infer(()),
                        ..
                    })
            )
            && fn_decl
                .inputs
                .iter()
                .all(|ty| matches!(ty.kind, hir::TyKind::Infer(())))
        {
            Applicability::MachineApplicable
        } else {
            Applicability::MaybeIncorrect
        };
```

We don't need the `Kind` enum here, we can just return the `msg` direclty:
```rust
let msg = match cx.typeck_results().expr_ty(recv).peel_refs().opt_diag_name(cx) {
    Some(sym::Option) => "unnecessary closure used to substitute value for `Option::None`",
    Some(sym::Result) => "unnecessary closure used to substitute value for `Result::Err`",
    _ => return,
};
```

